      "writtenOn": "2026-09-03T03:47:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1.Regarding reusing PLDM_OEM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_IANA:\nPLDM_OEM_FRU_FIELD_TYPE_IANA is defined inside libpldm/oem/ibm/fru.h (as part of pldm_oem_ibm_fru_field_type), which is conditionally included only under #ifdef OEM_IBM. Reusing it in the common/non-IBM path would require unconditionally including an IBM-scoped header in generic code or would break non-IBM builds (-Doem-ibm\u003ddisabled). Per DMTF DSP0257 Table 6, Field Type 1 is standard \"Vendor IANA\" across all OEM record sets, so keeping a generic constant (oemVendorIanaFieldType \u003d 1) avoids cross-vendor header dependencies.\n\n\n2.Done in Patchset 3. Hoisted the Vendor IANA mapping, uint32 IANA parsing, and raw hex fallback out of the #ifdef block so both paths share common logic, keeping only IBM-specific RT/IPZ handling guarded. Also trimmed the verbose comments.",
      "parentUuid": "f35c0779_15cde7b8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 189,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "ec8acccb6455448cee469794d72319b6bead7b26",
